{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/homeless-woman",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "homeless woman"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "A woman experiencing a specific, multidimensional existential and relational crisis, involving the severing of family ties and the trauma of domestic violence, which constitutes the main etiological factor of female homelessness."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "A characteristic defining element is the concept of hidden homelessness – women are less likely to exist on the street and more likely to live with loved ones or maintain dysfunctional relationships in exchange for shelter. Institutionally, this concept strongly correlates with homeless mother syndrome, determined by isolation in support facilities (e.g., single mothers' homes), a crisis in caregiving roles, and institutional anxiety. This phenomenon is operationally described by the European ETHOS classification, which categorises women's homelessness through the prism of lack of shelter, lack of housing, and existence in precarious or inadequate housing conditions."
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "3.5.1"
  ],
  "broader": {
    "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/homelessness",
    "prefLabel": {
      "en": "homelessness"
    }
  },
  "related": [
    {
      "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/domestic-violence",
      "prefLabel": {
        "en": "domestic violence"
      }
    },
    {
